# MDP, frequently asked
{.lead} The questions that come up most, collapsed so you can scan the headings and open only the one you need.

## What is a form?

A form is one output shape compiled from your source. The same content becomes a page, a deck, a flyer, and the interactive forms, with the design decided by the engine rather than the author.

---

## Do I write a separate file per form?

No. You write one `.mdp` source and list the forms you want:

- One source, many outputs.
- The renderer composes each form.
- Switching forms never touches your content.

---

## Can I change the colors?

The author picks a theme, not individual colors. That is the point: over-decorated output becomes structurally impossible.

:::callout tip
If you have a brand color, set `brand-accent` to a single hex. The engine derives an accessible accent set from it, in light and dark.
:::

---

## Which form should I use when?

| Need | Reach for |
| --- | --- |
| Read top to bottom | page or scroll |
| Present live | slides |
| Scan and jump | tabs or accordion |
| Walk through steps | stepper |

---

## Is the output accessible?

Yes. Every form ships semantic HTML, WCAG AA contrast, keyboard navigation, and a readable fallback when scripting is off.
